ruals":0.03575650549482625,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":6.6,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.14266989116149134,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":73.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.018401421591689532,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":77.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.012482833844706664,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.45862856396771906,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":23.6,"_gate_incr_roic":0.1173395542113122,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":55.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.06975261013483211,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":56.6,"_gate_pool_share":0.5516866971931418,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.0411433246188293,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":45.6,"_gate_margins":0.0014782693547399917,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":51.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0.015260070492219906,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":15.3,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.020692055424795436,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":34.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.005452722643458863,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":56.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009632426600909301,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":83.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.007929999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.143,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":14.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"nVent Electric plc designs, manufactures, markets, installs, and services electrical connection and protection solutions in the America, Europe, the Middle East, India, Africa, the Asia Pacific, and internationally. It operates in two segments, Systems Protection and Electrical Connections. The company provides solutions to protect electronics, systems, and data in mission critical applications, including data centers. It also offers solutions that connect power and data infrastructure. In addition, the company provides bus systems, cable management, control buildings, liquid and air-cooling solutions, electrical connections, enclosures, equipment protection, power connections, and power management solutions, switchgear systems, as well as tools and test instruments. The company markets its products through electrical distributors, retail, contractors, and original equipment manufacturers under the nVent CADDY, ERICO, HOFFMAN, ILSCO, SCHROFF, and TRACHTE brand names. Its products are used for various applications, such as industrial, commercial and residential, infrastructure, and energy. The company was founded in 1903 and is based in London, the United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Beth A. Wozniak | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 61 | Compensation: $3.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $324K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $31K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["nVent Electric plc is a large-cap industrials business with a $18.5B market cap on $3.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The business throws off $372M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.66\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 128% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.2837872823209138},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $11.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-11937360.34},{"text":"Significant goodwill (39% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Will Strong Q3 Earnings Change nVent Electric (NVT) Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-nvt/nvent-electric/news/will-strong-q3-earnings-change-nvent-electric-nvt-narrative","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794565717.409,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.743,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"(NVT) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/NVT_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_111226072601_1794529561.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794529561.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Recent Analysts\u2019 Ratings Changes for nVent Electric (NVT)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/recent-analysts-ratings-changes-for-nvent-electric-nvt.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794504417.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.052,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"nVent Electric (NYSE:NVT) Director Herbert Parker Buys 3,000 Shares of Company Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/nvent-electric-nysenvt-director-herbert-parker-buys-3000-shares-of-company-stock.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794355736.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.91,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"nVent Electric (NVT) Stock Looks Fairly Valued After Its 226% Run","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-nvt/nvent-electric/news/nvent-electric-nvt-stock-looks-fairly-valued-after-its-226-r","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794317225.85,